  Start the container with `bin/pulsar standalone --no-functions-worker --no-stream-storage` to avoid starting the functions worker and BookKeeper-backed stream storage, which aren't needed for basic producer/consumer coverage and would otherwise slow startup. Expose ports 6650 (client serviceUrl `pulsar://localhost:6650`) and 8080 (admin HTTP, usable for readiness polling, e.g. GET /admin/v2/clusters). Pulsar standalone takes substantially longer to become ready than nats/rabbitmq (it boots a broker, bookie, and ZooKeeper in one JVM), so the test must poll/retry for readiness with a generous timeout rather than reuse the short fixed sleep pattern seen in JnatsTest. Tear down the container (docker kill/rm) after the test so repeated local runs don't leak containers.
  
